# ── family content, kept out of a PUBLIC repo ────────────────────────────────
# Anchored with a leading slash, and that slash is the whole point: bare `photos/`
# matches ANY directory named photos at ANY depth — including
# app/api/backup/photos/, which is CODE. The photo-backup route was written,
# verified on localhost, reported as shipped, and never committed: Settings linked
# to a button that 404s in production. Verified with `git check-ignore -v`.
/photos/
/kids-starter.json
